===Etymology===
{{etymon|en|:inh|enm:brethen<ety:der<breeth>>}}
{{root|en|ine-pro|*bʰreh₁-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|brethen|t=to breathe, blow, exhale, odour}}, derived from {{der|en|enm|breth|t=breath}}. Eclipsed {{noncog|enm|ethien}} and {{m|enm|orðiæn}}, from {{noncog|ang|ēþian}} and {{m|ang|orþian|t=to breathe}}; as well as {{noncog|enm|anden}}, {{m|enm|onden}}, from {{noncog|non|anda|t=to breathe}}. More at {{l|en|breath}}.

