# {{senseid|en|omnidirectionally}} [[cast#Verb|Cast]] or [[scattered]] [[widely]] in all [[direction]]s; cast [[abroad]].
#: {{ux|en|The seed was '''broadcast''', not drilled.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=[[w:William Ellis (writer on agriculture)|William Ellis]]|chapter=Of White Oats|title=The Modern Husbandman: Or, The Practice of Farming: As it is Now Carried On by the Most Accurate Farmers in Several Counties of England. For the Month of April. [...]|location=Dublin|publisher=Printed by and for {{w|George Faulkner}}|year=1744|pages=48–49|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=JTBAAQAAMAAJ&pg=PA49|oclc=695977088|passage=And ſuch a double Sowing is of the greateſt Importance; for on the thick Growth of a Crop very much depends on the Bigneſs of it at Harveſt, becauſe, by ſuch a thick Growth, the Weeds are overcome and kept down from hurting the Oats; and, likewiſe, the Heats and Droughts kept the better out from parching up the Roots of the Oats, which, in too thin a Crop, often prove fatal to it; for, when Oats are ſown in the random or '''broadcaſt''' Way, there is no more Mold allowed their Roots than what the Harrows and Roll give them; which, at beſt, is but a ſuperficial and moſt thin Covering, and, therefore, the more liable to ſuffer by Droughts, which is different from the Way of ſowing Oats in Drills.}}
#* {{RQ:Song Chinese in Singapore|chapter=XII|page=444|passage=They alleged that, as soon as the Opium Commission was appointed, the various anti-opium organisations began to be extremely active and a determined campaign was carried on against the use of the drug by the circulation of a mass of anti-opium literature and the '''broadcast''' distribution of handbills and pamphlets.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=M. A. Mattoon|chapter=Application of Methods to Minimize Human Risks and Physical Dangers|title=Fire Handbook: Region Seven: {{w|United States Department of Agriculture}} [[w:United States Forest Service|Forest Service]]|location=Washington, D.C.|publisher=[[w:United States Government Publishing Office|Government Printing Office]]|month=June|year=1931|page=8|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=aOkJLWAm_6kC&pg=PA8|oclc=555361538|passage=There must be action on and participation in '''broadcast''' methods of public education, face to face, in groups, or by use of the mails. This, however, is of secondary importance to the man-to-man job of education in care with fire in the woods.}}
# [[communicate|Communicated]], [[signal#Verb|signalled]], or [[transmit]]ted to many people, through [[radio wave]]s or [[electronic]] means.
#: {{hypo|en|aired#Adjective|televised#Adjective}}
#: {{cot|en|narrowcast#Adjective}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=[[w:Charles-Marie Widor|Ch[arles]-M[arie] Widor]]|tlr=Edward Suddard|chapter=Percussion Instruments|title=The Technique of the Modern Orchestra: A Manual of Practical Instrumentation|edition=rev. and new|location=London|publisher=[[w:Stainer & Bell|Joseph Wiliams Limited]], 29, Enford Street, {{w|Marylebone}}, W.1|year=1946|oclc=852117766|newversion=reprinted|location2=Mineola, N.Y.|publisher2=w:Dover Publications|year2=2005|page2=208|pageurl2=https://books.google.com/books?id=1VgYi0mAxBgC&pg=PA208|isbn2=978-0-486-44269-3|passage=For radio-transmission it has been found that certain passages of a rhythmical nature come out more clearly if wooden-headed sticks are used. The Timpani sometimes tend to sound blurred and even to have a blurring effect on the rest of the orchestral ensemble in '''broadcast''' music, when ordinary soft sticks are used in a strongly marked rhythm.}}
# {{lb|en|attributive}} Relating to [[transmission]]s of [[message#Noun|messages]] or [[signal#Noun|signals]] to many people through radio waves or electronic means.
#* {{quote-web|en|author=Alina Selyukh|title=U.S. FCC eases foreign investment limit for broadcast stations|url=http://www.reuters.com/article/us-usa-fcc-foreigninvestment-idUSBRE9AD12F20131114|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20170816031730/http://www.reuters.com/article/us-usa-fcc-foreigninvestment-idUSBRE9AD12F20131114|archivedate=16 August 2017|work=w:Reuters|date=14 November 2013|passage=The new limitations would still prohibit foreigners from wholly or directly owning '''broadcast''' licensees, allowing only indirect ownership through a stake in a controlling parent of a '''broadcast''' licensee.}}

