#* {{quote-book|en|author=Robert E. Bartholomew|chapter=Introduction|mainauthor={{w|H. G. Wells|H[erbert] G[eorge] Wells}}|title=w:The War of the Worlds|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=Cosimo Books|year=2005|page=8|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=5-GoebU7DKwC&pg=PA8|isbn=978-1-59605-167-6|passage=The state of Rhode Island was the scene, on October 30, 1974, of yet another scare involving an adaptation of ''{{w|The War of the Worlds (radio drama)|The War of the Worlds}}''. '''Broadcast''' on radio station WPRO, Providence, the drama frightened listeners across the state. The play began with reporters covering a "meteor crash" near Jamestown, the purported Martian landing site. {{...}} City fire stations and other radio and TV outlets reported being inundated with inquiries from anxious callers, as was WPRO, which received more than a hundred calls.}}
