#* {{quote-song|en|title=w:OMG What's Happening|year=2020|author=w:Ava Max; {{w|Sorana (singer)|Sorana}}; Roland Spreckley; Henri Antero Salonen; w:Cirkut; Jason Gill|album={{w|Heaven & Hell (Ava Max album)|Heaven & Hell}}|artist=Ava Max|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hZ7Zw_ohxvU|text=I wanna tell you things and show you all the rest / '''Broadcast''' my emotions on the radio and take them off my chest / I hope you're listening / Are you?  Are you?}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To transmit a message over a wide area.
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Joseph Stalin|chapter=The October Revolution and the National Question|title=The October Revolution: A Collection of Articles & Speeches|series=Marxist Library|location=London|publisher={{w|Lawrence and Wishart|Martin Lawrence}}|year=[1934]|section=section III (The International Importance of the October Revolution)|pages=15–16|pageurl=https://archive.org/stream/in.ernet.dli.2015.183796/2015.183796.The-Octover-Revolution#page/n15/mode/1up/|oclc=254783389|passage=The break with imperialism and the liberation of Russia from the predatory war, the publication of the secret treaties and the solemn abrogation of the policy of seizing foreign soil, the proclamation of national freedom and the recognition of the independence of Finland, the declaration of Russia as a "Federation of Soviet National Republics" and the militant battle-cry of a resolute struggle against imperialism '''broadcast''' all over the world by the Soviet government in millions of pamphlets, newspapers, and leaflets in the mother tongues of the peoples of the East and West—all this could not fail to have its effect on the enslaved East and the bleeding West.}}
