====Usage notes====
The past of broadcast is either ''broadcast'' or ''broadcasted''.<ref>{{cite-web |en |url=https://www.merriam-webster.com/grammar/is-it-broadcast-or-broadcasted-forecast-or-forecasted-usage |title='Broadcast' or 'Broadcasted'? |publisher={{w|Merriam-Webster}} |work=Grammar & Usage |accessdate=2025-10-17|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260817153001/https://www.merriam-webster.com/grammar/is-it-broadcast-or-broadcasted-forecast-or-forecasted-usage|archivedate=17 August 2026}}</ref> Both are in use, but ''broadcast'' is much more common, especially in the simple past but also as past participle. As of 2019, Google Books search gives 326,000 results for [http://www.google.com/search?tbm=bks&tbo=1&q=%2B%22was+broadcast%22&btnG=Search+Books "was broadcast"], vs. 12,900 for [http://www.google.com/search?hl=en&tbo=1&tbm=bks&q=%2B%22was+broadcasted%22&aq=f&aqi=&aql=&oq= "was broadcasted"]. The influence of parallelism with {{m|en|cast#Verb|cast}} prevailing over ''casted'' is evident.

