The {{glossary|adjective}} is from {{inh|en|enm|bright}}, from {{inh|en|ang|berht}}, {{m|ang|beorht}}, {{m|ang|bryht}}, {{m|ang|byrht}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*berht}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*berhtaz|t=bright}}, ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*bʰerHǵ-|t=to gleam, shine, whiten}}.

The {{glossary|noun}} is derived from {{inh|en|enm|bright|t=brightness, brilliance; daylight; light}}, from {{m|enm|bright|pos=adjective}}:<ref>{{R:MED Online|pos=n|id=MED6030}}</ref> see above.
{{col-top|2|cog}}
Cognate with {{cog|sco|bricht|t=bright}}, {{cog|da|bjært|t=bright}}, {{cog|fo,is|bjartur|t=bright}}, {{cog|nn|bjart|t=bright}}, {{cog|sv|bjärt|t=bright}}, {{cog|got|𐌱𐌰𐌹𐍂𐌷𐍄𐍃|t=bright, clear; evident}}; also {{cog|cy|berth|t=beautiful, fair, fine}}, {{cog|sq|bardhë|t=white}}, {{cog|lt|brėkšti|t=to dawn}}, {{cog|pl|brzeżdżyć|t=to dawn}}, {{cog|ru|бре́зжить|t=to dawn}}, {{cog|fa|برازیدن|tr=barâzidan|t=to beautify; to befit}}.
{{col-bottom}}

