===Etymology 1===
{{etymon|en|:inh|enm:box<id:container>|id=container|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|box|id=container|t=container, box, cup}}, from {{inh|en|ang|box||box, case}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|part of speech=''n.''(2)|noformat=yes|id=MED5758|accessdate=23 August 2018}}</ref> from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*buhsā||box}} from {{der|en|la-lat|buxis||box}}, {{der|en|la|pyxis||small box for medicines or toiletries}}, of uncertain origin; compare {{cog|grc|πυξίς||box or tablet made of boxwood; box; cylinder}} and {{m|grc|πύξος||box tree; boxwood}}.<ref name="OED n2">Compare {{R:OED Online|part of speech=''n.''{{sup|2}}|noformat=yes|id=22297|date=1887}}</ref><ref>{{R:Online Etymology Dictionary}}</ref> {{doublet|en|piseog|pyx|pyxis}}.

Cognate with {{cog|dum|bosse}}, {{m|dum|busse||jar; tin; round box}} (modern {{cog|nl|bos||wood, forest}}, {{m|nl|bus||container, box; [[bushing]] of a wheel}}), {{cog|goh|buhsa}} ({{cog|gmh|buhse}}, {{m|gmh|bühse}}, modern {{cog|de|Büchse||box; can}}), {{cog|sv|bössa||box}}.<ref name="OED n2"/>

The humorous {{glossary|plural}} form {{m|en|boxen}} is from ''box'' + {{m|en|-en}}, by analogy with {{m|en|oxen}}.

{{sense|motor racing}} Used since it is more distinct over the radio compared to [[pit]]. Also from {{der|en|de|Boxenstopp||pit stop}}.

