##* {{quote-book|en|author=John Duncan|chapter=Rory Bremner|chapterurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=gcT_AQAAQBAJ&pg=PT35| title=Cricket Wonderful Cricket| location=London| publisher=[[w:John Blake (journalist)#John Blake Publishing|John Blake Publishing]]| year=2011| isbn=978-1-84358-316-5| passage=His &#91;{{w|Rory Bremner}}'s&#93; brilliant story about having his '''box''' turned inside out by a delivery from {{w|Jeff Thomson}}&nbsp;– he contrasts it with {{w|Andrew Flintoff}} being hit in the '''box''' by {{w|Cardigan Connor}}. [[w:David Lloyd (cricketer, born 1947)|[David] Lloyd]] came up to Flintoff, and said, "Cardigan Connor? You consider it an honour to be hit by Cardigan. Do you remember Jeff Thomson? I was hit amidships by him, and it was not a glancing blow. I was wearing one of those old '''boxes'''&nbsp;– you know, the pink ones, like a soap dish. It ended up that everything that was supposed to be inside the '''box''' had come outside the '''box'''&nbsp;– through the air holes!"}}
