##* {{quote-journal|en|author=Joe Holding, Rebecca Braybrook|title=What do DRS, black and white flag, porpoising and more mean? F1 terms explained|magazine=w:Autosport|url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/f1-terms-explained-what-box-marbles-drs-undercut-and-more-mean-5477591/5477591/|date=2024-04-03|passage=When a driver is told to ''''box''', '''box'''{{'}}, they're being instructed to make a pitstop. This is because ''''box'''{{'}} sounds more distinct than 'pit' over the team radio, so there's less chance of confusion leading to an error. The word itself refers to the painted box outside a team's garage where pit stops take place, although some argue that it hails from 'boxenstopp', which is German for 'pit stop'.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20241213194604/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/f1-terms-explained-what-box-marbles-drs-undercut-and-more-mean-5477591/5477591/}}
