===Etymology 3===
{{etymon|en|:inh|enm:box<id:blow>|id=blow}}
[[File:Fotos produzidas pelo Senado (30919118135).jpg|thumb|A woman practising boxing in [[Brazil]]]]

From {{inh|en|enm|box|id=blow|t=a blow; a stroke with a weapon}};<ref>{{R:MED Online|part of speech=''n.''(3)|noformat=yes|id=MED5759|accessdate=23 August 2018}}</ref> further origin {{unc|en|nocap=1}}, with relation<ref>{{R:OED Online|part of speech=''n.''{{sup|3}}|noformat=yes|id=22298|date=1887}}</ref> to {{inh|en|gem-pro|*boki-}}, whence {{cog|da|bask||a blow; a stripe}}, {{cog|da|baske|t=to flap, move around, beat violently}},  {{cog|dum|boke||a blow, a hit}}, {{m|dum|bōken||to slap, strike}} (modern {{cog|nl|beuken|t=to slap}}), {{cog|fy|bûkje}}, {{m|fy|bûtse}}, {{m|fy|bûtsje|t=to slap}}, {{cog|fy|-}} and {{cog|stq|batsje|t=to slap}}, {{cog|nds|betschen|t=to slap, beat with a flat hand}}, {{cog|gmh|buc||a blow, a stroke}}, {{m|gmh|bochen||to slap, strike}}, and further {{glossary|onomatopoeic}} shaping.

The verb is from {{inh|en|enm|boxen||to beat or whip (an animal)}}, which is derived from the noun.<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=boxen|part of speech=''v.''(2)|noformat=yes|id=MED5761|accessdate=23 August 2018|nodot=yes}}; {{R:OED Online|part of speech=''v.''{{sup|2}}|noformat=yes|id=22300|date=1887}}</ref>

