#* {{quote-book|en|year=1850|author=w:Thomas Keightley|title=The Fairy Mythology|location=London|publisher=H.G. Bohn|page=441|passage=Should any one attempt to fill his pockets, the money vanishes, and he is instantly assailed by a shower of '''boxes''' in the ear from invisible hands.}}

