===Etymology 4===
[[File:Boga Galiza.jpg|thumb|A '''box''' or [[bogue]] ({{taxfmt|Boops boops|species}}), a variety of [[sea bream]]]]
{{ety|en|id=fish|:der|la:bōx}}
From {{der|en|la|bōx}}, from {{der|en|grc|βῶξ||box (marine fish)}}, from {{m|grc|βοῦς||ox}} + {{m|grc|ὤψ||eye, view}}, a reference to the large size of the fish's eyes relative to its body.<ref>{{cite-book|chapter=Class IV.—PISCES.|title=Illustrations of Zoology.{{nb...|The Engravings by J[oseph] W[ilson] Lowry and Thomas Landseer, from Original Drawings by Sowerby, Varley, Holmes, Bone, Pyne, Lowry, and Charles Landseer; with Descriptive Letter-press Embracing a Systematic View of the Animal Kingdom, according to Cuvier, with Characteristic Anecdotes and Narratives Selected from the Works of Recent Naturalists.}}|location=London|publisher=Published by [[w:John Joseph Griffin|John Joseph Griffin and Co.]],{{nb...|53, Baker Street, Portman Square}}; Glasgow: [[w:Richard Griffin and Company|Richard Griffin and Co.]]|year=1851|page=112|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=nqoxAQAAMAAJ&pg=PA112|oclc=156769589|passage={{smallcaps|Boops.}} The eyes of the fish belonging to the genus are very large, whence the generic name from the Greek {{lang|el|βοῦς}}, ''an Ox'', and {{lang|el|ὤψ}}, ''an eye''.}}</ref>

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|dated}} A [[Mediterranean]] [[food fish]] of the [[genus]] ''[[Boops]]'', which is a [[variety]] of [[sea bream]]; a [[bogue]] or [[oxeye]].
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Albert Günther| chapter=Fam. 7. SPARIDÆ| title=Catalogue of Acanthopterygian Fishes in the Collection of the British Museum| location=London| publisher=Printed [by {{w|Taylor and Francis}}] by order of the trustees [of the {{w|British Museum}}]| year=1859| volume=I (Gasterosteidæ, Berycidæ, Percidæ, Aphredoderidæ, Pristipomatidæ, Mullidæ, Sparidæ)| page=418| pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=ec8MAQAAIAAJ&pg=PA418|oclc=853056837|passage='''BOX'''. '''Box''' (Boops), {{...}} In both jaws a single anterior series of broad incisors, notched at the cutting margin; no molars.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:William Yarrell| chapter=The Bogue|editor=[[w:John Richardson (naturalist)|John Richardson]]| title=Second Supplement to the First Edition of the History of British Fishes,{{nb...|[...] being also a First Supplement to the Second Edition.}}| location=London| publisher={{w|John Van Voorst}},{{nb...|Paternoster Row}}|year=1860|page=6|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=gzsDAAAAQAAJ&pg=PA6| oclc=7391853981| passage=The Bogue. {{...}} '''{{smallcaps|Box}}''' or {{smallcaps|Boops}}. ''Generic Character''.—Body elongated, rounded, the dorsal and ventral profiles alike, and the general aspect peculiarly trim.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Jonathan Couch| chapter=|title=A History of the Fishes of the British Islands| location=London| publisher=Groombridge and Sons,{{nb...|5, Paternoster Row}}| year=1862| volume=I| page=225| pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=MkYDAAAAQAAJ&pg=RA1-PA220| oclc=1046521752| passage=BOGUE. '''BOX'''. OXEYE. {{...}} In some parts of the European side of the Mediterranean the Bogue is a common fish, and where it frequents it is in great abundance.}}

