# {{senseid|en|tracts of land with largely wild vegetation; the vegetation itself}} {{lb|en|chiefly|Australia|New Zealand|South Africa|Canada|Alaska|often with “the”}} Tracts of land covered in natural vegetation that are largely [[undeveloped]] and [[uncultivated]], typically distinguished from absolute [[wilderness]] by implying a degree of marginal human engagement or proximity to settlement edges.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1779|author=Solomon Lovell|authorlink=w:Solomon Lovell|title=The Original Journal of General Solomon Lovell, Kept During the Penobscot Expedition, 1779: With a Sketch of His Life by Gilbert Nash|location=Weymouth, Mass.|publisher=Weymouth Historical Society|year_published=1881|page=102|passage=The Gentlemen took to the '''Bush''' and escaped being made prisoners.}}
