## {{senseid|en|Australia}}{{lb|en|Australia}} The [[countryside]] area of [[Australia]] that is less [[arid]] and less [[remote]] than the [[outback]]; ''loosely'', areas of natural flora even within [[conurbation]]s.
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1790|author=Ralph Clark|authorlink=w:Ralph Clark|title=Journal|url=https://www.sl.nsw.gov.au/sites/default/files/2025-12/Transcription%20of%20Ralph%20Clark%27s%20journal.html|passage=(Davis) my Convict Servant who was in the Boat with me begd of me not to goe on Shore he is one of the greatest Cowards living I cald to them again when I got to ther fire for the[y] had run into the '''bush''' on there Seing the Boat pulling towards them}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1894|author=w:Henry Lawson|chapter=We Called Him "Ally" for Short|title=Short Stories in Prose and Verse|url=http://gutenberg.net.au/ebooks06/0607911.txt|passage=I remember, about five years ago, I was greatly annoyed by a ghost, while doing a job of fencing in the '''bush''' between here and Perth.}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1899|author={{w|Ethel Pedley|Ethel C. Pedley}}|title=w:Dot and the Kangaroo|url=http://gutenberg.net.au/ebooks09/0900681h.html|passage=Little Dot had lost her way in the '''bush'''.}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=2000|author=Robert Holden; Paul Cliff; Jack Bedson|title=The Endless Playground: Celebrating Australian Childhood|pageurl=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=XX4YnwQACqIC&pg=PA16&dq=%22the+bush%22+-intitle:%22bush%22+-inauthor:%22%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=z5AVT5WxIYaTiAe94MlD&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22the%20bush%22%20-intitle%3A%22bush%22%20-inauthor%3A%22%22&f=false|page=16|passage=The theme of children lost in the '''bush''' is a well-worked one in Australian art and literature.}}
##* {{quote-web|en|url=https://www.australianherald.com/news/271027691/australian-farmers-under-pressure-from-climate-change|title=Australian farmers under pressure from climate change|date=2021-09-06|work=Australian Herald|passage=The findings of the Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change suggest Australia may have to jettison tracts of the '''bush''' unless there is a massive investment in climate-change adaptation and planning.|accessdate=7 September 2021|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20210907131527/https://www.australianherald.com/news/271027691/australian-farmers-under-pressure-from-climate-change|archivedate=7 September 2021}}
